{"assets":["/statement-assets/18c238b79503bf6fa11530b4095c8de3e1d475a8649e0c6afb812b1ca611cd7e.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"495","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Digital Counter"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Malek lives in an apartment block with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"100"},{"kind":"text","text":" floors numbered from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"99"},{"kind":"text","text":". The apartment has an elevator with a digital counter showing the floor that the elevator is currently on. The elevator shows each digit of a number with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"7"},{"kind":"text","text":" light sticks by turning them on or off. The picture below shows how the elevator shows each digit."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/18c238b79503bf6fa11530b4095c8de3e1d475a8649e0c6afb812b1ca611cd7e.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One day when Malek wanted to go from floor "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"88"},{"kind":"text","text":" to floor "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":" using the elevator he noticed that the counter shows number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"89"},{"kind":"text","text":" instead of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"88"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then when the elevator started moving the number on the counter changed to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"87"},{"kind":"text","text":". After a little thinking Malek came to the conclusion that there is only one explanation for this: One of the sticks of the counter was broken. Later that day Malek was thinking about the broken stick and suddenly he came up with the following problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Suppose the digital counter is showing number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". Malek calls an integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ x ≤ 99"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if it's possible that the digital counter was supposed to show "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" but because of some(possibly none) broken sticks it's showing "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" instead. Malek wants to know number of good integers for a specific "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". So you must write a program that calculates this number. Please note that the counter "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"always"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" shows two digits."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of input contains exactly two digits representing number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ n ≤ 99"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Note that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" may have a leading zero."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the only line of the output print the number of good integers."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"89\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"00\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"73\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"15\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample the counter may be supposed to show "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"88"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"89"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample the good integers are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"00"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"08"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"80"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"88"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third sample the good integers are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"03, 08, 09, 33, 38, 39, 73, 78, 79, 83, 88, 89, 93, 98, 99"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"495A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/495/problem/A"}